# Pin the mirror control files to LF regardless of core.autocrlf.
# CRLF here silently defeats the exclusion parsing and leaks private files
# into the public GitHub mirror (see devops/post_squash_hook.sh).
devops/git_mirror_exclusions.txt                text eol=lf
devops/git_mirror_content_filters.txt           text eol=lf
devops/git_last_mirror_commit_ids_registry.txt  text eol=lf

# Every shell script in the tree, not just the mirror ones above.
#
# core.autocrlf is true by default on Windows and is set globally on this
# machine, so without this a fresh clone checks these out with CRLF. That is
# not cosmetic: a CRLF shebang reads as '#!/usr/bin/env bash\r', which is not
# an interpreter, and the failure is reported as exit 127 with no clue as to
# why. src/version.c.sh is the first thing the build runs, so a CRLF checkout
# fails before a single source file is compiled.
#
# Covers version.c.sh, dev_build.sh, tests/run_generator_test.sh and every
# fixture under tests/fixtures/.
*.sh                                            text eol=lf
